        <mxCell id="9og8Tt8GYBWu8dkJrYvM-124" value="Network Access" style="rounded=1;fillColor=#23445D;gradientColor=none;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontFamily=Tahoma;fontSize=14" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="850" y="340" width="190" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9og8Tt8GYBWu8dkJrYvM-133" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;VPC lets you provision a logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud where you can launch AWS resources in a virtual network that you define.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;dashed=1;perimeterSpacing=0;perimeter=centerPerimeter;align=left;spacingRight=5;spacingLeft=5;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="120" y="438" width="180" height="540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9og8Tt8GYBWu8dkJrYvM-134" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; line-height: 100%; font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Subnets are chunks of IP addresses in your VPC that allow you to group resources together.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;dashed=1;perimeterSpacing=0;perimeter=centerPerimeter;align=left;spacingRight=5;spacingLeft=5;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="355" y="438" width="180" height="540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9og8Tt8GYBWu8dkJrYvM-135" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;- public with Internet gateway(IGW)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- private with Virtual private gateway (VPN)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- more private with AWS Direct Connect&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;dashed=1;perimeterSpacing=0;perimeter=centerPerimeter;align=left;spacingRight=5;spacingLeft=5;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="605" y="440" width="180" height="540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9og8Tt8GYBWu8dkJrYvM-136" value="&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Network Access Control List (ACL)&lt;/b&gt;:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Network ACLs check traffic going into and leaving a subnet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EC2 Security Group&lt;/b&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;controls the traffic that is allowed to reach and leave the resources&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The key difference between a security group and a network ACL is the security group is stateful, meaning, as we talked about, it has some kind of a memory when it comes to who to allow in or out, and the network ACL is stateless, which remembers nothing and c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;dashed=1;perimeterSpacing=0;perimeter=centerPerimeter;align=left;spacingRight=5;spacingLeft=5;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="857" y="438" width="180" height="562" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tsMgJcmONPBiCTRYHQR3-128" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;dashed=1;dashPattern=1 1;glass=1;shadow=1;backgroundOutline=0;autosize=0;treeFolding=0;treeMoving=0;shadowColor=#FFFF66;sketch=1;curveFitting=1;jiggle=2;strokeWidth=3;strokeColor=#B5739D;flipH=1;flipV=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1100" y="320" width="200" height="700" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tsMgJcmONPBiCTRYHQR3-129" value="Domain Name System&#xa;DNS" style="rounded=1;fillColor=#23445D;gradientColor=none;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontFamily=Tahoma;fontSize=14" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1103" y="340" width="190" height="80" as="geometry" />
